Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::the_clock_divider_is_total`.

The defect: the bypass test is strict, so a target equal to the base gets divider 1 and the card
runs at half the rate it could, while the bypass is never taken for the one rate it fits.

Expected to fail: `assert!((divider == 0) == (base <= target))`, at a target equal to the base.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/host_controller.rs
@@ -165,7 +165,7 @@ pub const fn clock_divider(base_hertz: u32, target_hertz: u32) -> Option<u8> {
     if target_hertz == 0 {
         return None;
     }
-    if base_hertz <= target_hertz {
+    if base_hertz < target_hertz {
         return Some(0);
     }
     // ceil(base / (2 * target)). Saturating, and still exact: a target of 2^31 or more saturates
